From 048c469acc61f1db5c31b0496cf1d023d12ffb96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Marcelo Poblete (via Claude)" <marcelopoblete.us@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 00:50:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: auto-numbered tags no longer collide and lose the drawn
 route
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Drawing a route failed with "duplicate key value violates unique
constraint fiber_routes_project_id_route_id_tag_key" and the route was
lost. R-014 had just been created; the next draw asked for R-014 again.

The tag was auto-numbered in the browser from the copy of the project
it last loaded, while (project_id, tag) is UNIQUE in the database.
Anything that makes the browser's copy stale — a second tab, a refresh
that hadn't landed, another user on the same project — produces a tag
that already exists, and the insert is rejected outright.

The tag is now resolved server-side against live data, with the
browser's tag treated only as a preference, and the insert retries on a
unique violation (up to 5 times) in case the tag is taken in the gap
between reading and writing. Applied to both fiber routes and fiber
nodes; the mirrored conduit run, conduit structure, cabinet, cable and
enclosure tags all derive from the resolved tag rather than the one the
browser suggested, so they stay consistent.

Renaming a route keeps reporting a duplicate as an error — there the
user picked the name on purpose and should see the clash.

Verified the numbering against this project's real tags, including the
"R-004 existing " style names with trailing text.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ScqTACWd5u51GDZPenDDdM
